ELECTROMAGNETIC PURIFICATION OF ENDOCYTIC VACUOLES AND ACIDOSOMES FROM
DICTYOSTELIUM

Harish Padh

Center for Biotechnology, Northwestern University, 2153
Sheridan Road, Evanston, IL 60208, Tel: 708-467-1453, Fax:
708-467-2180, E-mail: padh@nwu.edu

ABSTRACT

   Earlier studies have shown that, in Dictyostelium discoideum, ~90%
of the vacuolar proton pump (V-H+-ATPase) activity is present in a
buoyant membrane fraction called 'acidosomes'.  In the presence of
Mg2+, acidosomes and endocytic vacuoles copurified on equilibrium
sucrose gradients suggesting their reversible association.  The
association depended on Mg2+ and cytosolic proteins (1,2).  To further
characterize the putative association of acidosomes and endocytic
vacuoles, cells were fed dextran-coated superparamagnetic iron colloid
plus FITC-dextran to load and label their endocytic vacuoles.  The
endocytic vesicles were then purified ~20-fold at >60% yield by their
retention on a column of fine steel wire in an electromagnetic field
in the absence of Mg2+.  The fraction retained on a magnet column
contained only about 5% of total cellular V-H+-ATPase and traces of
other organelle markers.  In the presence of 1.5 mM Mg2+, however, the
retention of V-H+-ATPase as well as FITC-dextran was ~60% with only
traces of contaminant markers.  When such preparations were washed
with buffer lacking Mg2+ while still in the magnetic field, the
endocytic marker (FITC-dextran) remained on the column while
V-H+-ATPase was eluted selectively.  The elute was shown by
negative-stain electron microscopy to contain purified acidosomes
(saccular membranes studded with V-H+-ATPase).  The parent material,
recovered from the column in the presence of Mg2+, was rich in
endocytic vacuoles bearing colloidal iron.  In an electron microscope,
the endocytic vacuoles were often seen associated with pump-studded
acidosomes.  The results independently support and extend earlier
observation that acidosomes and endocytic vacuoles physically
associate in a Mg2+-dependent manner.  In addition, the procedure
provides a rapid method to purify acidosomes.

